  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Unsettled weather will persist throughout this \nweek with daily chances of showers and thunderstorms.\n\nA broad upper level ridge across the Southeast with surface high\npressure offshore should keep advecting warm and humid air \nthroughout this week. Precipitable water values will continue to\nremain elevated with amounts over 1.5 inches. Meanwhile, a \nbroad upper level trough should cross the Great Lakes and reach\nthe Northeast by the middle of this week. This overall pattern \nwill allow showers and thunderstorms to develop across the \nAppalachian Mountains each afternoon. While forcing appears weak\ntoday, a passing cold front to the north will provide more lift\nduring Tuesday and Wednesday. As a result, both days feature an\nincreased risk of severe thunderstorms due to damaging winds \nand localized flash flooding from heavy rainfall. Confidence in \nthese risks is highest along and west of the Blue Ridge. \nAlthough convective activity diminishes a little in intensity \nand coverage towards the end of this week, sufficient \ninstability and orographical lift will ensure that storm chances\nlinger throughout the upcoming weekend.",
